# Credentials of a Ubisoft account, used to authenticate against Ubisoft's
# (unofficial) API via r6api.js. Use a throwaway / secondary Ubisoft account,
# NOT your main account — this can be against Ubisoft's Terms of Service and
# may get the account flagged.
#
# Copy this file to ".env.local" and fill in the values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# === Recommended: R6Data (https://r6data.com) ===============================
# A hosted service that fetches the official R6 data for you behind an API key.
# This avoids the Ubisoft login entirely (no DataDome, no 2FA, no per-IP login
# rate limit) and works from any network and when deployed. Get a free key at
# https://r6data.com and paste it here. When set, the app uses R6Data and the
# UBI_* / DataDome settings below are not needed.
R6DATA_API_KEY=

# === Alternative: direct Ubisoft (unofficial) API ==========================
# Only used when R6DATA_API_KEY is empty. Requires Ubisoft account credentials,
# is blocked by DataDome on many networks, and rate-limits logins per IP.
UBI_EMAIL=your-ubisoft-email@example.com
UBI_PASSWORD=your-ubisoft-password

# Ubisoft protects its login with DataDome (anti-bot). To get past the 403,
# copy a `datadome` cookie value AND the matching User-Agent from a browser
# where you are logged in to ubisoft.com (both from the SAME browser):
#   1. Log in at https://account.ubisoft.com in Chrome.
#   2. DevTools (F12) -> Application -> Cookies -> https://...ubi.com
#      -> copy the value of the cookie named "datadome".
#   3. DevTools -> Console -> type: navigator.userAgent  -> copy the string.
# Paste them below (no quotes). The cookie expires after a while; refresh it
# when you start getting 403s again.
R6_DATADOME=
R6_USER_AGENT=
